      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To determine the number of women who attended the party, we can use the information given about the number of men and the number of women who danced with them.\n\nFirst, let's denote the number of women who attended the party as \\( w \\).\n\nWe know that each man danced with exactly 3 women, and there are 12 men. Therefore, the total number of \"man-woman dance pairs\" (or \"man-woman interactions\") can be calculated by multiplying the number of men by the number of women each man danced with:\n\\[\n12 \\text{ men} \\times 3 \\text{ women per man} = 36 \\text{ man-woman dance pairs}\n\\]\n\nNext, we know that each woman danced with exactly 2 men. Therefore, the total number of \"man-woman dance pairs\" can also be calculated by multiplying the number of women by the number of men each woman danced with:\n\\[\nw \\text{ women} \\times 2 \\text{ men per woman} = 2w \\text{ man-woman dance pairs}\n\\]\n\nSince both calculations represent the same total number of dance pairs, we can set them equal to each other:\n\\[\n36 = 2w\n\\]\n\nTo find \\( w \\), we solve the equation by dividing both sides by 2:\n\\[\nw = \\frac{36}{2} = 18\n\\]\n\nThus, the number of women who attended the party is \\(\\boxed{18}\\).",
