    "text": "To determine the number of women who attended the party, we can use the information given about the number of men and the number of women who danced with them.\n\nFirst, let's denote the number of women who attended the party as \\( w \\).\n\nWe know that each man danced with exactly 3 women. Since there were 12 men, the total number of \"man-woman\" dances (or pairings) can be calculated as:\n\\[\n12 \\text{ men} \\times 3 \\text{ women per man} = 36 \\text{ dances}\n\\]\n\nNext, we know that each woman danced with exactly 2 men. Therefore, the total number of \"man-woman\" dances can also be expressed as:\n\\[\nw \\text{ women} \\times 2 \\text{ men per woman} = 2w \\text{ dances}\n\\]\n\nSince the total number of dances is the same in both expressions, we can set them equal to each other:\n\\[\n36 = 2w\n\\]\n\nTo find \\( w \\), we solve the equation by dividing both sides by 2:\n\\[\nw = \\frac{36}{2} = 18\n\\]\n\nThus, the number of women who attended the party is \\(\\boxed{18}\\).",
